Subject: screensaver: run on Debian, without ttfx and without a qterminal veto

Omarchy's screensaver never ran on this box at all, for two separate reasons,
and both are in the launcher.

The first is `ttfx`. omarchy-launch-screensaver opens with

    if omarchy-cmd-missing ttfx; then exit 1; fi

and ttfx is an AUR package -- a Rust text-effects renderer with no Debian
package and no Debian equivalent. On Kali that guard is unsatisfiable, so the
launcher exited 1 every time it was called: on idle, from the menu, from
`omarchy-launch-screensaver force`. Nothing was broken and nothing was
logged; the feature was simply absent.

The second is the terminal. The launcher only proceeds if the system's
default terminal is Alacritty, Foot, Ghostty or Kitty, because it needs to
pass a window class (so the `org.omarchy.screensaver` fullscreen rule
matches) and a font size. On a stock Kali `xdg-terminal-exec --print-id`
reports qterminal, which takes neither -- the same limitation that patch 0002
works around for presentation terminals. So even with a renderer in place the
launcher would have refused.

This patch changes both:

  * the ttfx requirement becomes a kali-screensaver requirement, and the
    terminals run `kali-screensaver` instead of `omarchy-screensaver`.
    kali-screensaver is this repo's renderer -- a scene animation rather than
    a text-effect engine, so it is a replacement for ttfx rather than a port
    of it, and it draws Kali's own dragon burning a castle.

  * the terminal check falls back to whichever of the four IS installed
    rather than refusing outright. Being unable to name a window is a reason
    to use a different terminal for this one window, not a reason to have no
    screensaver. Kitty is preferred and is already installed by
    10-omarchy4-packages.sh.

Everything else is left alone deliberately. The per-monitor loop, the socat
event stream that waits for each window to map before moving focus, the
screensaver-off toggle and the `force` argument all still work, so idle
detection, `omarchy-toggle-screensaver`, the bar's idle indicator,
omarchy-debug-idle and omarchy-system-lock's cleanup keep functioning
unchanged -- they all address the screensaver through the same
`org.omarchy.screensaver` window class.

--- a/bin/omarchy-launch-screensaver	2026-09-15 13:08:15
+++ b/bin/omarchy-launch-screensaver	2026-09-15 13:08:28
@@ -2,7 +2,10 @@
 
 # omarchy:summary=Launch the Omarchy screensaver in the default terminal on the system with the correct font configuration.
 
-if omarchy-cmd-missing ttfx; then
+# Kali: the screensaver here is kali-screensaver, not ttfx. ttfx is an AUR
+# package with no Debian equivalent, so on Kali the stock guard exited 1 every
+# time and the screensaver never ran at all.
+if omarchy-cmd-missing kali-screensaver; then
   exit 1
 fi
 
@@ -17,10 +20,28 @@
 focused=$(omarchy-hyprland-monitor-focused)
 terminal=$(xdg-terminal-exec --print-id)
 
+# Kali: if the default terminal is not one of the four, fall back to whichever
+# of them IS installed instead of refusing. The screensaver needs a terminal
+# that takes a window class and a font size on the command line; qterminal,
+# which is what xdg-terminal-exec reports on a stock Kali, takes neither. That
+# is a reason to use a different terminal for this one window, not a reason to
+# have no screensaver.
 case $terminal in
 *Alacritty* | *ghostty* | *foot* | *kitty*) ;;
 *)
-  omarchy-notification-send -g ✋ "Screensaver only runs in Alacritty, Foot, Ghostty, or Kitty"
+  for candidate in kitty alacritty foot ghostty; do
+    if command -v "$candidate" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+      terminal=$candidate
+      break
+    fi
+  done
+  ;;
+esac
+
+case $terminal in
+*Alacritty* | *alacritty* | *ghostty* | *foot* | *kitty*) ;;
+*)
+  omarchy-notification-send -g ✋ "Screensaver needs Alacritty, Foot, Ghostty, or Kitty installed"
   exit 1
   ;;
 esac
@@ -57,17 +78,17 @@
   hypr_focus_monitor "$m"
 
   case $terminal in
-  *Alacritty*)
-    hypr_exec alacritty --class=org.omarchy.screensaver --config-file "$OMARCHY_PATH/default/alacritty/screensaver.toml" -e omarchy-screensaver
+  *Alacritty* | *alacritty*)
+    hypr_exec alacritty --class=org.omarchy.screensaver --config-file "$OMARCHY_PATH/default/alacritty/screensaver.toml" -e kali-screensaver
     ;;
   *ghostty*)
-    hypr_exec ghostty --class=org.omarchy.screensaver --config-file="$OMARCHY_PATH/default/ghostty/screensaver" --font-size=18 -e omarchy-screensaver
+    hypr_exec ghostty --class=org.omarchy.screensaver --config-file="$OMARCHY_PATH/default/ghostty/screensaver" --font-size=18 -e kali-screensaver
     ;;
   *foot*)
-    hypr_exec foot --app-id=org.omarchy.screensaver --config="$OMARCHY_PATH/default/foot/screensaver.ini" -e omarchy-screensaver
+    hypr_exec foot --app-id=org.omarchy.screensaver --config="$OMARCHY_PATH/default/foot/screensaver.ini" -e kali-screensaver
     ;;
   *kitty*)
-    hypr_exec kitty --class=org.omarchy.screensaver --override font_size=18 --override window_padding_width=0 -e omarchy-screensaver
+    hypr_exec kitty --class=org.omarchy.screensaver --override font_size=18 --override window_padding_width=0 -e kali-screensaver
     ;;
   esac
 
